{"name":"Blue Suede Shoes","hex":"#484b62","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"suede","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of soft leather, made from calfskin, with a brushed texture to resemble fabric, often used to make boots, clothing and fashion accessories."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of suede."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suede"},{"term":"shoes","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of shoe"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of shoe"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Suede Shoes","blocks":[{"text":"\"Blue Suede Shoes\" is a rock and roll standard written and first recorded by American singer, songwriter and guitarist Carl Perkins in 1955. It is considered one of the first rockabilly records, incorporating elements of blues, country and pop music of the time. Perkins' original version of the song appeared on the Cashbox Best Selling Singles list for 16 weeks and spent two weeks at the number two position."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Blue_Suede_Shoes_Carl_Perkins.png/330px-Blue_Suede_Shoes_Carl_Perkins.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Suede_Shoes","wikidata":"Q885912"},{"title":"Blue Suede Shoes (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Suede Shoes is a 1980 music documentary film directed by Curtis Clark and produced by Don Boyd with Penny Clark that combines archival film of early American rock 'n' roll pioneers of the 1950s and British singers Cliff Richard and Tommy Steele with material recorded at a 1979 rock 'n' roll revival weekender featuring bands and people following the scene."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Suede_Shoes_(film)","wikidata":"Q25136601"},{"title":"Suede","blocks":[{"text":"Suede is a type of leather with a fuzzy, napped finish, commonly used for jackets, shoes, fabrics, purses, furniture, and other items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Blue_suede_samba.JPG/330px-Blue_suede_samba.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suede","wikidata":"Q1071417"},{"title":"Shoe","blocks":[{"text":"A shoe is an item of footwear normally found in pairs intended to protect and comfort the human foot, usually made in such a way that one is designed to fit the left foot and the other the right foot."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Skor_fr%C3%A5n_1700-_till_1960-talet_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0056302.jpg/330px-Skor_fr%C3%A5n_1700-_till_1960-talet_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0056302.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoe","wikidata":"Q22676"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Inspiration_for_the_song_%22Blue_Suede_Shoes%22.jpg/330px-Inspiration_for_the_song_%22Blue_Suede_Shoes%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Inspiration_for_the_song_%22Blue_Suede_Shoes%22.jpg/330px-Inspiration_for_the_song_%22Blue_Suede_Shoes%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shoes in Elvis exhibit similar to those that inspired the song","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fi